{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1559708-some-ideas-on-order-of-reason-exploratory-society-combat-guilds","id":1559708,"title":"Some ideas on Order of Reason Exploratory Society combat guilds","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2026-05-02T18:55:30-07:00","id":1559708,"title":"Some ideas on Order of Reason Exploratory Society combat guilds","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Border Corps Division\u2019s history began long ago. The ancient Seekers rarely traveled alone; the spaces between human civilizations were vast, untamed, and filled of danger. That danger was part of why the Seekers ventured out in the first place, but there was little point to exploring if you didn\u2019t survive to tell what you\u2019d discovered. Seekers struck out with retinues of various sizes, and always included folks good in a fight. By the time of the Convention of the Ivory Tower, these soldiers and bodyguards organized themselves into several autonomous guilds. They determined which Seeker expedition or Celestial Master enclave would get which group of stalwart defenders.<br /> <br /> Over time, the guilds evolved into rigid models based along military lines. Sometimes they took their nom de guerre from a decorated and charismatic leader, such as Hawking\u2019s Rifles (a legendary mercenary group during the Napoleonic wars). Other times, they were descended from renowned military groups, like the vaunted Burmese and Nepalese Ghurkas. These units had rivalries, friendly and otherwise \u2014 stiff competition has always been a hallmark of militant groups in closely overlapping fields of operation. The Grand Housecleaning of Queen Victoria put an end to all that, in theory. The newly formed Technocratic Union ordered the guilds to organize into one larger unit, branded the Border Corps Division. </div> </div> </div>Many famous military groups have served as escorts/guards for Seekers and Celestial Masters. These diverse guilds of elite military groups, often competitive among themselves, were only unified into a single methodology after the Grand Housecleaning. The text cites the Hawking's Rifles and the Gurkhas as examples, both of which share the commonality of being military groups established after the 18th century. Prior to that, during the Renaissance and the Early Modern period, what kind of military groups do you think would have taken on the role of escort forces?<br /> <br /> A guild of plate-armored, pike-shot \u201cconstellations\u201d<br /> A guild of uhlans/cossack/hussar light cavalry<br /> A guild of Luminary cuirassiers and pistoliers<br /> A guild piloting war-palace galleons<br /> A guild of fervent duelists, preference for slender and thrust-centric weapons<br /> A guild manufacturing Da Vinci contraptions for war<br /> Church militants armed with star-flanged maces<br /> Slave soldiers and sellsword companies<br /> <br /> Do you think these guilds/private militaries are thematically appropriate for the Seekers and the Celestial Masters? If you have any other ideas, please feel free to share them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11780,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11780-posthumanity","user":"Posthumanity","date":". 05-03-2026, 07:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11780-posthumanity","name":"Posthumanity","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"220"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}